In it's infinite wisdom, Dell has started shipping a new variant of
the SB live value - they call it the SB live 5.1(whatever), creative
model # CT0200.

It is _not_ a standard emu10k1 chipset.

Is anyone on the list working with this beast?  If so, do you need some
help?  If not, can anyone point me at tech docs for this card?

The rc7 alsa release at least recognizes the card, but throws gnome
into fits during use - our mixer app segfaults and dies somewhere in
the gnome sound event handler...

We're stuck using these things, and I'm the poor schmuck stuck with the
driver development work for it...

Thanks in advance...




